rota lap 4356, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; read as its own sense, walking the fence line of mantra/src/weave.rye and pressing each post rather than reading what the posts claim
think Merge and annotate had landed since the baton's text was written, and both are rostered green -- so the lane's next work was not where the seat prompt pointed. Ran all six lane witnesses first: all GREEN.
think Pressed the bounds. merge, annotate, apply and current each carry a measured cost table and each was repaired within the last two days, so the quadratics are gone and the ceilings serve.
think The post that gave way was a stated one. `Weave.merge`'s doc names four postcondition properties; its assert loop holds three. The one that passes is `line.run < merged.next_run` -- the third of the three counter invariants the `Weave` type declares at line 422, and the field `Place.less_than` compares FIRST.
think Two things rest on it: the next apply stamps its whole insert block with next_run and appends, and current reads the backing list without sorting. Both arguments are spelled in current's own header and both cite APPLY's postcondition, which does assert all three -- so the reasoning stood on a post existing on one path into a weave and not on the merge path. from_v1 carried the same gap.
obs The merge assert is isolating, proven from both sides on metal: the control's new run_counter phase rewrites the counter's @max to @min, exiting 134 with the assert and 0 without it while every other witness claim passes. The from_v1 assert is a RESTATEMENT and says so in its own comment -- the lift witness's `lifted.next_run == 1` catches that plant either way, measured the same way.
obs The pin could not hold the row. construction/REDS.md stood 226 bytes under its 40,960 bound with thirteen OPEN rows, so no lap could book a red at all, and the header reserves the raise to Keaton's word. Folded the two BOOKED rows (%643, a peer's, and %644, mine) onto one shelf with the rostered loom, which gave the pin 4,422 bytes back for the fleet.
obs Three reds on the cold roster, all closed: reds_ledger_headline (my row's arithmetic, repaired by its own write tool), declared_ceiling (the fold), fold_shelf_link_repoint (two depth-lost links in a peer's shelf from an hour before, repaired by the rostered repointer).
obs Grade on the touched module is C+ -- register 83, truth 100, reach 60 against a Door budget of 9. Measured before and after the edit and unmoved: it is a property of 618 words of dense module header rather than of this lap's ten lines. A reach molt of the whole header is its own round.
